# Optional file-system policy, chosen by whoever compiles (stdlib/fs.caspien: Dir/File). No keys = no restriction.
#
# fs-roots: the directories a program may open BY PATH, with access (r = read-only, rw = read-write); paths use '/'. With this key set,
#   `Dir.root("/literal")` / `Dir.rootRW(..)` are checked at compile time (the literal must be a root or below one, no '..', and rw only in
#   an :rw root); a computed path must go through `new RootPath(path)`, which checks the same table at run time; anything else needs
#   `unsafe file{ Dir.rootAny(path) }`. Without the key every path is accepted.
# fs-deny-externs: extern names (or @link_name targets) that code outside stdlib/ may not declare, so the stdlib's Dir/File is the only way in.
#   `java Compiler ... --fs-report` lists every path open and every `unsafe file` use the compiler saw.
#
# fs-roots: /var/app/data:rw, /var/app/config:r
# fs-deny-externs: open, openat, creat, fopen, freopen, unlink, unlinkat, rename, renameat, mkdir, mkdirat, rmdir, chdir, symlink, link
